tunproxy (0.3.0~rc2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stop importing arbitrary non-default unicast routes into the bypass policy.
  * Limit dynamic bypass entries to active interface host addresses.
  * Reject unspecified interface and upstream addresses.

 -- TunProxy Maintainers <maintainers@tunproxy.invalid>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0800

tunproxy (0.3.0~rc1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Always bypass local, private, link-local, multicast, and broadcast ranges.
  * Preserve existing non-default routes and the selected SOCKS5 upstream path.
  * Add a read-only command that shows the active internal bypass policy.

 -- TunProxy Maintainers <maintainers@tunproxy.invalid>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0800

tunproxy (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add an unprivileged CLI and a socket-activated privileged daemon.
  * Allow Ubuntu sudo-group administrators to use daily commands without sudo.
  * Preserve configuration and verified cores during in-place package upgrades.
  * Keep the proxy disabled after fresh installation and package upgrades.
  * Harden daemon capabilities and clear them from download and verification
    tools.
  * Document installation, in-place updates, reinstall, and removal behavior.

 -- TunProxy Maintainers <maintainers@tunproxy.invalid>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800

